# No cluster deploy — fail this application repo if a workflow deploys straight
# to a cluster (issue #1206, epic #1058; the position is #1189).
#
# The infrastructure repo is the only path to a cluster: an application repo
# publishes versioned, immutable images and never touches a cluster itself, and
# a version change reaches the cluster as a pull request against the
# infrastructure repo. This job runs scripts/check-no-cluster-deploy.zsh over
# .github/workflows/** and fails on a step whose `run:` body invokes a
# cluster-WRITING command. The checker's header states the full command set, all
# THREE exemptions — a job that stands up its own ephemeral kind/k3d/minikube/
# ctlptl cluster, job-scoped (covering the steps at or after it, the rest of the
# creating step's own body included) — keyed on the EARLIEST creator in the job
# and its condition, so an unconditional one exempts every cluster-writing step
# at or after it, while a creator carrying an `if:` guard exempts only a step
# carrying the byte-identical condition, because the branch-per-environment
# shape (`if: pull_request` stands up kind, `if: ref == main` deploys) is
# exactly what this gate exists to catch, so a differing condition fails closed;
# a single COMMAND carrying a REAL dry-run
# value — bare `--dry-run`, `--dry-run=client|server|true`, or `--dry-run
# client|server`, but NOT `--dry-run=none` / `--dry-run=false`, which mean the
# opposite — command-scoped, NOT the whole step; and, repo-wide, a
# `.maintenance.yml` recording `primary: kubernetes` —
# and why there is deliberately no escape hatch.
#
# UNCONDITIONAL TRIGGER — no `paths:` / `paths-ignore:` filter, on purpose. This
# check is a REQUIRED context in branch protection, and required status checks
# resolve by NAME: GitHub leaves a required check in the `expected` state
# forever when the workflow that defines it was skipped by a path filter, so a
# path-conditional required check wedges every PR that doesn't touch the paths.
# Running unconditionally is affordable because the job is a static scan of
# .github/workflows/** needing only zsh, jq and a pinned yq — no build, no
# container, no cluster.
#
# Generated by /development:bootstrap. Source template:
# development/skills/bootstrap/templates/common/.github/workflows/no-cluster-deploy.yml.tmpl
name: no-cluster-deploy

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: ["{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}"]
  workflow_dispatch: {}

permissions:
  contents: read

concurrency:
  group: no-cluster-deploy-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true

jobs:
  no-cluster-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 10
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@df4cb1c069e1874edd31b4311f1884172cec0e10 # v6

      - name: Install checker toolchain (jq + zsh; a pinned yq from upstream)
        env:
          # mikefarah yq, NOT Debian's `yq` apt package (kislyuk's python-yq is
          # a different query language with no `-o=json` and YAML 1.1
          # semantics). Pinned: an unpinned download makes this required check's
          # verdict depend on whatever upstream released this morning.
          YQ_VERSION: 4.44.3
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          sudo apt-get update -qq
          sudo apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends jq zsh >/dev/null
          sudo curl -sSfLo /usr/local/bin/yq \
            "https://github.com/mikefarah/yq/releases/download/v${YQ_VERSION}/yq_linux_amd64"
          sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/yq

      - name: Scan workflows for direct-to-cluster deploy steps
        run: zsh scripts/check-no-cluster-deploy.zsh
